        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This section provides general information, not tax advice. Consult a qualified tax professional for guidance specific to your situation and jurisdiction.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-ink mt-8 mb-3">Self-employment basics</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">In most countries, Canvas UGC creators are classified as independent contractors, not employees. This means you're responsible for reporting and paying your own taxes. In the US, you'll receive a 1099 form if you earn over $600 from a single program. In the EU, you'll typically need to register as a freelancer or sole trader.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-ink mt-8 mb-3">Deductible expenses</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">As a self-employed creator, you can typically deduct business-related expenses from your taxable income. Common deductions include:</p>
        <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-2 mb-4">
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[140px]">Equipment:</strong> Camera, microphone, lighting, tripod, phone</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[140px]">Software:</strong> Editing tools (CapCut Pro, Premiere, etc.), cloud storage</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[140px]">Internet:</strong> Percentage of your internet bill used for work</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[140px]">Home office:</strong> Portion of rent/mortgage if you have a dedicated workspace</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[140px]">Props &amp; supplies:</strong> Products purchased for content creation</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-ink mt-8 mb-3">Record keeping</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Keep detailed records of all income and expenses from your first payment. Use a spreadsheet or accounting tool to track monthly earnings by program, platform, and payment method. Save receipts for all business purchases. Good records now save hours of stress at tax time &mdash; and potentially thousands in missed deductions.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display text-[18px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-ink mt-8 mb-3">International creators</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">If you're creating Canvas UGC for brands in a different country, you may need to complete tax treaty forms (like W-8BEN for US-based programs). Payment processing fees for international transfers (PayPal, Wise) are also deductible as a business expense. Factor these fees into your earnings calculations when comparing program offers.</p>
